    <string name="wallpaper_permission_note">Uses its own rhythm by default. Turn on real audio in settings if you want it to follow what is playing.</string>
    <string name="settings_visualizer_real_audio">Visualiser follows real audio</string>
    <string name="settings_visualizer_real_audio_summary">Off by default. On, it reads what the device is playing and needs the record-audio permission, which lights the microphone indicator. Off, it runs on its own invented rhythm and asks for nothing.</string>
    <string name="visualizer_permission_needed">Record-audio permission is needed for that</string>
    <string name="visualizer_choice_title">How should it react?</string>
    <string name="visualizer_choice_message">This wallpaper can follow whatever your phone is playing, or move to a rhythm of its own.\n\nFollowing real audio needs the record-audio permission. It reads the sound your phone is playing, not your microphone, but Android asks with the same dialog either way and the microphone indicator will show.\n\nIts own rhythm needs no permission at all and most people cannot tell the difference.</string>
    <string name="visualizer_choice_ambient">Its own rhythm</string>
    <string name="visualizer_choice_real">Follow real audio</string>
    <string name="visualizer_falling_back">No permission, so it will use its own rhythm. You can change this in Eden settings.</string>

